Fixed and committed as e2bb480 (Fixes #1210). git commit -m "kill -9 1 at $(date)" no longer asks at the REPL and is no longer refused in a sub-agent. Anything inside $(...) or backticks in the message is still checked and still refused. fmt, clippy -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass.

What changed
• The #1196 echo/printf rule in bash_parse.rs now also covers message values. For git commit that's -m, --message, --message=, glued -m"…", -am and repeated -m, and it works after git -C dir / git -c k=v using the same option list the existing git check uses. For gh it's --body, -b, --title and -t.
• Both checks in that layer read the message as a mention now: the plain-text scan and the parse-tree scan.
• One deviation from the plan: the task said gh with any subcommand. I only covered the built-in issue, pr and release. A gh extension or shell alias can pass -b text to a shell, so those stay checked.
• These still ask, each confirmed refused at HEAD first and pinned in a test:
  • a command chained after the message (&& rm …)
  • piping git's output (| sh)
  • other git options and commands: -F file, a path after --, git merge -m
  • sudo git, /usr/bin/git
  • gh api -f body=, a gh extension
  • interpreter bodies: python3 -c, bash -c, node -e

Evidence
• Before/after table: 33 generated triggers, one per safety check, in 8 argv slots, old code vs new. 18 triggers flip from refused to allowed in each of the 5 message slots, and nothing else flips in either direction. The echo, python3 -c and git merge -m controls are unchanged. I posted the table on #1210 before committing.
• Recall control: I disabled the new code with a NEUTERED marker (count 1 before the run) and the new test failed by name. Restored (count 0), all 9 tests passed.
• Built-binary probe: it can't show this change. In -p mode there's no confirmation step, so these warnings are logged quietly and the command runs. HEAD's binary and the new one both ran the specimen with no warning. I compared the two places this verdict actually shows up (the REPL check and the sub-agent refusal) directly: HEAD refused the specimen, the new build allows it.

Found along the way, filed separately
• #1222: a phrase inside an interpreter string literal (python3 -c, the Day-266 incidence) is still refused. yoyo can't tell a Python string from code that runs.
• #1223: the hard block (the one --yes can't override) still refuses git commit -m "fix rm -rf / at $(date)". It also refuses echo "rm -rf / at $(date)", so the gap predates #1196. Once a $( appears, that check deletes the quotes and the mentioned text reads as a command. It's a different layer, so it isn't in this diff.
• While writing #1222, the hard block refused my own heredoc that quoted the phrase. That's the #1102 shape, and I logged the incidence there.

The docs line that said these mentions "can still ask (#1210)" in troubleshooting/safety.md is rewritten, and its pointers now go to the open #1222 and #1223. safety.rs shrank by one line and its entry in tests/module_size.rs is updated.

